{
  "dom_id": "step-q140897",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $Q$ is an $n\\times m$  matrix\n- $\\text{Col}(A)$ is spanned by the columns of $Q$\n- $R$ is a $m\\times m$ matrix",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. $Q$ should be an $m\\times n$ matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A),$ they span $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\n- Statement III is false. $R$ must be an $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
